            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MargoAnn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "No ginger? No white wine? My recipe is better and only 5 ingredients: Soy sauce, white sugar, white wine, garlic and you must have ginger.",
            "datePublished": "2024-05-19T15:13:17.399Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Peter"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is excellent on any kind of meat. My favourite is to use this marinade with pork tenderloin. Put the meat and marinade overnight , I usually do it on the bbq using a cookina. It is a family and friends favourite.",
            "datePublished": "2024-05-19T15:07:16.444Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Scott"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great marinade and is a dead ringer for the taste of my local Chinese food restaurant beef teriyaki... I added 1/2 the juice and skin from a clementine orange to the mix. Then I boiled the mixture and then let cool before using. It’s a long extra step but in my opinion well worth the effort!",
            "datePublished": "2020-02-21T13:27:14.330Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amber Brown"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I'm allergic to soy, so I used equal parts South River Miso chickpea tamari and Coconut Aminos instead of the soy sauce. Added minced ginger instead of cinnamon, and used beef broth instead of water. Skipped the sugar. Placed pork chops in it overnight, and they came out amazing. I boiled the marinade for 10 minutes then used it to make stir fry veggies with soft noodles. Perfect meal.",
            "datePublished": "2014-12-06T18:18:54.110Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kschroppel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Didn’t have cinnamon so used ground ginger. Delicious!!",
            "datePublished": "2024-05-20T00:09:16.234Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "mschuckles"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Quick, easy and marinates in a half hour. Great flavor. I now use ginger instead of cinnamon as cinnamon doesn't agree with my husband. Delicious!!",
            "datePublished": "2022-10-10T20:48:48.113Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "dianeschmidtks"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I doubled the recipe and left out the ginger and cinnamon. I added 1 tsp of corn starch per recipe (so 2 tsps in this case). I would ad 3 - 4 tsps or a tbsp and then more if needed. I cut a steak into thin slices and marinated it, then served the beef with teriyaki over steamed rice and broccoli. My teenagers liked it too. Will definitely make it again! It was quick, easy, and really tasty!",
            "datePublished": "2015-09-02T19:32:08.887Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "tstuck"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Tasty and simple. I'm saving this one. Made it exactly to the recipe and my wife liked it so much she suggested having guests for dinner using this recipe. We cut up a pork tenderloin and used it for kabobs with red bell peppers, mushrooms and zucchini. Marinated the meat for a for about six hours using 1/2 the mixture and the veggies for about 1/2 hour using the remainder and grilled for about 12 minutes turning after 5 minutes and again 4 minutes later. Next time I use this recipe I might add a 1/4 tsp of cayenne for a little kick and adding onions to the kabob mix. Also, I will use 1/3 of the mix for the meat marinade and 2/3 for the veggies as there is about twice as much veg to meat. We will try this with chicken and pork chops also.",
            "datePublished": "2013-05-19T19:11:44.197Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lindsay McClain Opiyo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was so easy and so delicious. Made for veggie and chicken kabobs. I boiled leftover marinade and used as a sauce over coconut rice.",
            "datePublished": "2020-06-08T02:18:09.450Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Stefani"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious and easy! I added 2 large cloves of garlic (minced) to the marinade before marinading boneless chicken breasts for 3 hours. The biggest compliment came from my son who said the chicken tasted \"just like the chicken at Chinese restaurants!\"",
            "datePublished": "2008-08-06T15:58:01.453Z"
          },
          {
